        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "977c86e7-58f8-5492-956c-e9b08f655c07",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Carolina, Puerto Rico; San Juan; Montrose, Colorado\n- Airports: Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport; Montrose Regional Airport\n- Codes: IATA SJU, ICAO TJSJ, FAA LID SJU; IATA MTJ, ICAO KMTJ, FAA LID MTJ\n- People: Luis Muñoz Marín\n- Concepts: joint civil-military airport; non-towered public airport\n\nFacts:\n- Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport is an international joint civil-military airport in suburban Carolina, Puerto Rico, 3 miles southeast of San Juan.\n- Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport uses the codes IATA SJU, ICAO TJSJ, and FAA LID SJU.\n- Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport is also known in Spanish as Aeropuerto Internacional Luis Muñoz Marín and as Isla Verde International Airport or Aeropuerto Internacional de Isla Verde.\n- Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport is named for Luis Muñoz Marín, Puerto Rico's first democratically elected governor.\n- Montrose Regional Airport is a non-towered public airport on the northwest side of Montrose in ZIP code 81401 in southwestern Colorado.\n- Montrose Regional Airport uses the codes IATA MTJ, ICAO KMTJ, and FAA LID MTJ.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
